{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), giving us a baseline for the RNA modality but no information about whether image features carry useful signal. The highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design question right now is whether the image modality is informative at all, because this determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing or whether we should focus on improving the RNA pipeline. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly answers this: it isolates image signal with a standard, well-understood encoder. Comparing its accuracy to the 48.5% RNA baseline will tell us (a) whether image features are competitive, (b) whether they are complementary (motivating multimodal experiments), or (c) whether they are weak (redirecting budget toward RNA encoder/aggregation improvements). ResNet50 is chosen over ViT-L because it is the encoder used in the multimodal configs, making the single-modality result a direct ablation reference. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential architectural decision (modality choice) before committing budget to more complex multimodal or encoder-variant experiments."
}

